[2026-11-18T12:15:17.993Z] [DEBUG] [rpc] github←resp 6744b {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"icons":[{"mimeType":"image/png","src":"data:image/png;base64,","theme":"light"},{"mimeType":"image/png","src":"data:image/png;base64,","theme":"dark"}],"name":"github-mcp-server","title":"GitHub MCP Server","version":"v2.1.0"}},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"additions\":62,\"base\":{\"ref\":\"main\",\"repo\":{\"description\":\"Open EV and charging-network data for Charge Line, kept current by GitHub Agentic Workflows with Claude\",\"full_name\":\"Suv4o/charge-line-data\"},\"sha\":\"[REDACTED]\"},\"body\":\"The first preview runs signed in to Claude and ran, but did little. This fixes what got in their way.\\n\\n| Problem in the previews | Fix |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| WebFetch failed with \\\"Unable to verify if domain is safe to fetch\\\": Claude Code checks each domain with claude.ai first, and that check can't leave the sandbox | Skip the check (`skipWebFetchPreflight`) and let the firewall decide. It now allows `*.com.au`, `*.gov.au`, `*.org.au`, `*.net.au`, The Driven, Open Charge Map and makers' `.com` sites, and blocks the do-not-read sites outright |\\n| Chained shell commands (`cd …; python3 …`) were refused, and the catalogue agent stopped | The shared rules now say how to use the tools: files through Read/Edit/Write, one shell command at a time, and a refused command is never a reason to stop |\\n| The memory folder path in the instructions was wrong | `/tmp/gh-aw/repo-memory/\\u003cid\\u003e/` |\\n\\nBoth agents stay in staged mode: the next runs are previews again.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\"changed_files\":5,\"closed_at\":\"2026-11-18T10:53:42Z\",\"commits\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-11-18T10:12:24Z\",\"deletions\":17,\"draft\":false,\"head\":{\"ref\":\"fix/agent-tools\",\"repo\":{\"description\":\"Open EV and charging-network data for Charge Line, kept current by GitHub Agentic Workflows with Claude\",\"full_name\":\"Suv4o/charge-line-data\"},\"sha\":\"[REDACTED]\"},\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/Suv4o/charge-line-data/pull/5\",\"mergeable_state\":\"unknown\",\"merged\":true,\"merged_at\":\"2026-11-18T10:53:42Z\",\"merged_by\":\"Suv4o\",\"number\":5,\"state\":\"closed\",\"title\":\"Agents: let WebFetch through the firewall, one shell command at a time\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-11-18T10:53:45Z\",\"user\":{\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56303591?v=4\",\"id\":56303591,\"login\":\"Suv4o\",\"profile_url\":\"https://github.com/Suv4o\"}}"}],"structuredContent":{"additions":62,"base":{"ref":"main","repo":{"description":"Open EV and charging-network data for Charge Line, kept current by GitHub Agentic Workflows with Claude","full_name":"Suv4o/charge-line-data"},"sha":"[REDACTED]"},"body":"The first preview runs signed in to Claude and ran, but did little. This fixes what got in their way.\n\n| Problem in the previews | Fix |\n| --- | --- |\n| WebFetch failed with \"Unable to verify if domain is safe to fetch\": Claude Code checks each domain with claude.ai first, and that check can't leave the sandbox | Skip the check (`skipWebFetchPreflight`) and let the firewall decide. It now allows `*.com.au`, `*.gov.au`, `*.org.au`, `*.net.au`, The Driven, Open Charge Map and makers' `.com` sites, and blocks the do-not-read sites outright |\n| Chained shell commands (`cd …; python3 …`) were refused, and the catalogue agent stopped | The shared rules now say how to use the tools: files through Read/Edit/Write, one shell command at a time, and a refused command is never a reason to stop |\n| The memory folder path in the instructions was wrong | `/tmp/gh-aw/repo-memory/\u003cid\u003e/` |\n\nBoth agents stay in staged mode: the next runs are previews again.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","changed_files":5,"closed_at":"2026-11-18T10:53:42Z","commits":1,"created_at":"2026-11-18T10:12:24Z","deletions":17,"draft":false,"head":{"ref":"fix/agent-tools","repo":{"description":"Open EV and charging-network data for Charge Line, kept current by GitHub Agentic Workflows with Claude","full_name":"Suv4o/charge-line-data"},"sha":"[REDACTED]"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Suv4o/charge-line-data/pull/5","mergeable_state":"unknown","merged":true,"merged_at":"2026-11-18T10:53:42Z","merged_by":"Suv4o","number":5,"state":"closed","title":"Agents: let WebFetch through the firewall, one shell command at a time","updated_at":"2026-11-18T10:53:45Z","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56303591?v=4","id":56303591,"login":"Suv4o","profile_url":"https://github.com/Suv4o"}},"resultType":"complete"}}
