https://thedriven.io/2026/07/02/new-leapmotor-b05-electric-hatchback-to-land-in-australia-from-35990-driveway/): \"$39,990 for the Design LR\", \"67.1kWh LFP\", \"up to 482km\", \"fast charging up to 174kW\", \"18 minutes\", \"11kW AC\" |\n| `alfa-romeo-junior-2025` wltpKm | 398 → 407 | [Alfa Romeo Australia Junior](https://www.alfaromeo.com.au/models/junior) (18 Nov 2026): \"54kWh\", \"407km (WLTP)\", \"100kW DC Charging\" |\n| `fiat-500e-2023` untilYear | — → 2026 | Stellantis told The Beep that the cars \"have now largely been sold through\" and it is \"not planning additional orders\" (July 2026). abarth.com.au is now a parked domain. |\n| `abarth-500e-2023` untilYear | — → 2026 | As above |\n\nEvery new or changed entry has `checked: 2026-11-18`. The file's `updated` date is 2026-11-18.\n\n### Things I wasn't sure about\n- **Deepal E07:** Deepal shows prices only through a postcode tool, so the fetch saw \"From XX,XXX RDP\". I counted it as on sale because the page says \"Test drives are available now at your local retailer\" and dealers list stock (e.g. $77,704 drive-away in Queensland). I used body `suv` for this SUV-ute \"multitruck\"; `ute` is arguable. The year is 2025 because dealer listings say MY25.\n- **Leapmotor B05:** the figures come from The Driven, which credits the price to Leapmotor. leapmotor.net/au failed with a certificate error in the sandbox. I added only the Design LR. I left out the Style because its peak DC is unclear: The Driven gives \"up to 174kW\" for the range, and another listing gives 156 kW.\n- **MG U9:** \"102.2kWh\" isn't labelled gross or usable, so I estimated usable at 99 kWh.\n- **Alfa Junior:** the range now comes from the maker page. Its charging notes say \"Overseas model shown, Australian specification may vary\", so I left the existing charge estimate as it was.\n- **Fiat and Abarth end of sale:** this comes from a Stellantis quote reported by The Beep, not from a maker page; fiat.com.au returned 403.\n\n### Not done this run\n- **Re-checked (6):** BYD, Abarth, Alfa Romeo, Deepal, Denza and Fiat. BYD's battery-electric range and the Denza D9 match the file.\n- **Not re-checked:** Tesla, Audi, BMW, Cadillac, Cupra and Ford. Their AU sites returned 403, timed out or failed the certificate check, and tesla.com is off-limits. They are left undated so the next run takes them first.\n- **ROVER:** couldn't be read. Its list loads from content.powerapps.com, which fails the certificate check in the sandbox.\n- **BITRE:** the sheets didn't download (timed out).\n- **Kept as candidates:** HQ/Hongqi E-HS9 (only an indicative price below $150k, deliveries from Jan 2027), Avatr 07L/06T (expressions of interest only), Denza Z9 GT (no AU price) and the Chery E5 (see the separate issue).\n\nNo page asked me to do anything outside the task.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","branch":"catalogue/2026-11-18-u9-x9-e07-b05","title":"Add the MG U9 EV, Xpeng X9, Deepal E07 and Leapmotor B05; Alfa Junior range; Fiat and Abarth 500e no longer sold new"},"name":"create_pull_request"}}
